# A FAILED Slack delivery must never write the webhook to a log (banshee-a4i).
# reqwest's error Display includes the request URL, and for this sink the URL IS the
# credential — so a bare `%e` persists the webhook into ~/Library/Logs on every failed
# POST. The test asserts on CAPTURED LOG OUTPUT, because neither reading the source nor
# checking that delivery fails quietly can tell `%e` from `%e.without_url()`.
file: rust/banshee-api/src/slack.rs
test: a_failed_delivery_never_logs_the_webhook_secret
---OLD---
                tracing::warn!(error = %e.without_url(), "could not deliver escalation alert to Slack");
---NEW---
                tracing::warn!(error = %e, "could not deliver escalation alert to Slack");
